device.description:
Nimbus found this in your Energy Dashboard and your price providers:

{bindings}

Keep it ticked to include it. You can change any of it later in Configure.

finish.description:
Nimbus will set up:

{devices}

It fills in the settings these imply, and keeps this device setup beside them (shadow) until you choose to put it in charge. The Solver tab's Device setup card then shows what works now and what still needs one more fact. Control of your battery stays off.

device_setup_dry_run.description:
Built from your current settings, the device setup is **{result}**.

{details}

Nothing is changed by reading this. When it is clean, tick below to keep the device setup alongside your settings (shadow): your settings stay in charge.

frozen_price_input.description:
These price settings point at a rate that is fixed when the forecast is built and never revised (LocalVolts Rate All Var). On 9 Oct 2026 such a rate stayed near 13c while the live price reached $1.32, so the plan never saw the spike:

{inputs}

Point them at the live price instead: for LocalVolts, Buy Flex Up and Sell Flex Up, and Flex Up Forecast for the price array. This message clears itself once fixed.

non_power_unit_power_input.description:
These settings need a power sensor (W or kW), but the sensor reports another unit, so Nimbus is reading its number as kW, which is wrong:

{inputs}

Amps (A) are current, not power, and kVA is apparent power. Pick the matching power sensor in Nimbus → Configure, or reconfigure the controllable load, battery, Load or Power Signal. This message clears itself once fixed.

energy_unit_power_input.description:
These settings point at an energy counter (Wh/kWh), but Nimbus needs a power sensor (W or kW):

{inputs}

Pick the matching power sensor (most inverters and meters expose both) in Nimbus → Configure, or reconfigure the Load / Power Signal. This message clears itself once fixed.

placeholder_settings.description:
These are still at the 0.1 placeholder a new install starts on, so the plan is for a tiny battery or grid connection, not yours:
{settings}

Set your real values on the Nimbus dashboard's **Solver tab → Basic settings** (the card named on each line). This message clears itself once they are set.

plan_failing_infeasible.description:
Since {since}, on each of the last {cycles} cycles, the solver proved that no plan meets your current settings (the solver's reason: {reason}). Until this clears, the plan Nimbus publishes schedules no battery or load activity.

{causes}

While this lasts, the battery forecast's `status` attribute reads `infeasible`. This clears itself on the next good plan.
